{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LevelMapValuation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMapValuation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L283-L309","doc":"**The quadratic degree bound.** A nonzero coefficient joining\nMasbaum level `n` to block level `m` satisfies\n\n`2·deg c ≥ 2n(n+1) + 3m(m+1)`,\n\ni.e. `deg c ≥ n(n+1) + 3m(m+1)/2` — **quadratic in both indices**, not\nlinear. This supersedes `natDegree_ge_of_bridge_combined` (whose\n`2n+3m` reads only the `q = 1` vanishing); the full Pochhammer product\ncarries every cyclotomic factor.\n\nConsequence: the reachable region under a degree budget `D` shrinks\nfrom `O(D²)` pairs to `O(D)` — `n ≲ √D` and `m ≲ √(2D/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_qPochC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_qPochC","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L269-L281","doc":"`deg (q;q)_n = n(n+1)/2`, stated doubled to stay in `ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L262-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_succ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_succ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L258-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.one_sub_X_pow_succ_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.one_sub_X_pow_succ_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L252-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow_succ","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L247-L250","doc":"`1 − X^{k+1}` has degree `k+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_unbounded_of_all_levels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_unbounded_of_all_levels","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L228-L245","doc":"**No bounded-degree level map bridges the tail.** If a level map\nintertwines at *every* Masbaum level with nonzero coefficients, then its\ncoefficient degrees are unbounded: for any budget `D` some level needs\na coefficient of degree exceeding `D`.\n\nSo there is no \"small\" universal bridge. Any level-mixing map valid at\nall orders has coefficients whose complexity grows without bound —\nwhich is a structural fact about the surviving family, obtained without\nsearching it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.level_le_of_natDegree_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.level_le_of_natDegree_le","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L218-L226","doc":"**A degree budget caps the reachable Masbaum level.** If the\ncoefficient joining level `n` has degree at most `D`, then `2n ≤ D`:\nonly levels `n ≤ D/2` are reachable, whatever `m` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_of_bridge_combined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_of_bridge_combined","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L203-L216","doc":"**The sharpened degree bound.** A nonzero coefficient joining\nMasbaum level `n` to block level `m` has degree at least `2n + 3m`.\n\nBoth indices cost. Demanding more orders of the tail pushes `n` up,\nand each unit of `n` costs two more degrees of coefficient — so a\nlevel map whose coefficients are drawn from any fixed bounded-degree\nfamily covers only a finite triangle of `(n, m)` pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_of_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_ge_of_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L191-L201","doc":"**Degree bound.** A nonzero level-`m` bridge coefficient in `ℤ[X]`\nhas degree at least `3m`. Consequence: coefficients drawn from any\nbounded-degree family reach only finitely many levels — the module map\ncannot be arbitrary, which is precisely the narrowing the B1.5 design\nnote asked for before any check is run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L184-L189","doc":"`(1 − X)^k` has degree `k` in `ℤ[X]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_eq_qPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC_eq_qPoch","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L173-L176","doc":"`qPochC` is `HabiroTailStar.qPoch`'s formula — the two agree\ndefinitionally wherever both typecheck. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPoch_prod_dvd_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPoch_prod_dvd_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L146-L165","doc":"**The full-product constraint — strictly stronger than the\n`(1 − q)`-adic one.** The `(1 − q)^{2n+3m}` bound above only reads off\nthe vanishing at `q = 1`; but the *entire* Pochhammer product divides\nthe coefficient. Since\n`(q;q)_k = ∏_d Φ_d^{⌊k/d⌋}` ranges over every cyclotomic factor, this\ncaptures the constraint at **every** root of unity at once, not just at\n`q = 1`.\n\nIts degree consequence is quadratic rather than linear\n(`natDegree_ge_quadratic`), which shrinks the reachable region from\n`O(D²)` pairs to `O(D)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_coeff_combined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_coeff_combined","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L125-L144","doc":"**The sharpened constraint.** Both sides contribute: the block's\norder-`3m` pole must be paid for, *and* the Masbaum level term already\nvanishes to order `2n`. So the forced coefficient carries\n`(1 − q)^{2n + 3m}`, not merely `(1 − q)^{3m}`.\n\nThis is strictly stronger than `sub_one_pow_dvd_coeff_single_level`\n(which is the `n = 0` case) and it is the bound that matters: the\nMasbaum index `n` is the one that runs when more orders are demanded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_masLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_masLevel","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L115-L123","doc":"The Masbaum level term `C_n·(q;q)_n²` is itself divisible by\n`(1 − q)^{2n}` — its Pochhammer sits in the numerator, so it\n*contributes* vanishing at `q = 1` rather than consuming it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.no_single_level_of_not_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.no_single_level_of_not_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**The pruning form (contrapositive).** A coefficient that misses the\ndivisibility rules its level out — no scan required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_coeff_single_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_coeff_single_level","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L90-L106","doc":"**The derived constraint.** If a single GGM block level `m` carries\nthe whole bridge — `mas · (q;q)_m³ = c · num` with the block numerator\n`num` a unit (as it is on the `j = 0` row, a monomial) — then the\ncoefficient is forced to carry `3m` factors of `(1 − q)`.\n\nThis is what pole cancellation costs: the block's order-`3m` pole at\n`q = 1` must be paid for by the coefficient, since the Masbaum side is\nregular there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_qPochC_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_qPochC_cube","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L84-L88","doc":"`(1 − q)^{3m} ∣ (q;q)_m³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_qPochC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.sub_one_pow_dvd_qPochC","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L70-L82","doc":"`(1 − q)^m ∣ (q;q)_m`: each factor `1 − q^{j+1}` is divisible by\n`1 − q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LevelMixing.qPochC","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LevelMapValuation.lean#L64-L68","doc":"`(q;q)_m = ∏_{j=1..m} (1 − q^j)` over a generic commutative ring —\nthe same formula as `HabiroTailStar.qPoch`, at the weaker typeclass the\ndivisibility statements need (see the header: over a field they would\nbe vacuous). ","signatureChunk":0}]}